{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Whatever has fins and scales — these you may eat.</b> The reason for the fins and scales is that the creatures that possess them always dwell in the upper regions of the waters and in their clear depths, and they receive nourishment from the air that enters there; therefore they possess a certain heat that repels from them the influx of moistures, just as wool and hair, and also nails, do in man and beast. But that which has no fins and scales always dwells at the bottom of the waters and in their murky depths, and because of the excess of moisture and the gathering of cold, it cannot repel anything from itself; therefore they possess a cold moisture close to being deadly, and it is indeed deadly in certain bodies of water, in stagnant pools. Thus wrote the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:41.750337628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}